taking the postgresql as the example: 

Probe               Simple meaning            What Happens if it fails?

startupProbe        Has PostgreSQL finished   After the 30 consecutive failures,
                    starting                  kubernetes restart the container

readinessProbe      Can PostgresSQL accept     Kubernetes marks the pods as not ready 
                    connection 

livenessProbe       Is the postgreSQL still    kubernetes restart the containers after 
                    responding                 the configured failure threshold is reached


++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++

                    # Checks whether PostgreSQL has started successfully.
startupProbe:
  exec:
    command:
      - sh
      - -c
      - pg_isready -U "$POSTGRES_USER" -d "$POSTGRES_DB"
  failureThreshold: 30  # Allow up to 30 consecutive failures before restarting the container.
  periodSeconds: 5      # Run the check every 5 seconds.

# Checks whether PostgreSQL is ready to accept database connections.
readinessProbe:
  exec:
    command:
      - sh
      - -c
      - pg_isready -U "$POSTGRES_USER" -d "$POSTGRES_DB"
  periodSeconds: 10     # Run the check every 10 seconds.
  timeoutSeconds: 5     # Wait up to 5 seconds for each check to complete.

# Checks whether PostgreSQL is still healthy.
livenessProbe:
  exec:
    command:
      - sh
      - -c
      - pg_isready -U "$POSTGRES_USER" -d "$POSTGRES_DB"
  periodSeconds: 20     # Run the check every 20 seconds.
  timeoutSeconds: 5     # Wait up to 5 seconds for each check to complete.
